diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 3c96a7172..b7108e117 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -99,6 +99,8 @@ For a deployable Cluster LLServer package, use `./build.sh --nexus-cluster-serve
 
 Cluster permission revision synchronization is opt-in at build time with `-p:EnableClusterIntegration=true`. Cluster instances require the per-instance `LANCER_NEXUS_GAME_INSTANCE_KEY` and the internal Redis `LANCER_NEXUS_PERMISSION_REDIS_ENDPOINT=host:port`. LLServer reports `IsReady=false` until it has subscribed to Redis, loaded and activated the current Gateway SQL permission snapshot, and received its revision ACK. Redis carries invalidations only; a disconnected listener makes the instance unready. Standalone builds remain independent of Cluster.
 
+After a clustered player selects a character, LLServer resolves its stable Gateway ID, acquires its fenced lease, and loads the latest Gateway SaveGame snapshot. If that character has no snapshot yet, the existing local SQLite row is imported once as revision 1. LLServer checkpoints the live SaveGame to Gateway every minute, persists explicit Freelancer saves, and writes a transferred SaveGame under the target lease fence after transfer commit. Gateway validates each read and write against the active instance, session, lease token and version. Character creation/deletion and durable persistence on an unclean process stop still need integration; do not treat the local SQLite bootstrap as the cluster persistence authority.
+
 ## NPC retirement recovery infrastructure
 
 Patch 1126 adds a durable background retirement outbox under the configured NPC
